How microservices  communicate -

1) Synchronous- (RestTemplate, RestClient - without spring cloud, FeignClient- for spring cloud)

* RestTemplate - legacy way to call RestAPIs in spring app
limitations - 
1) so many overloaded methods, so hard to maintain 
2) it was built before concepts like retry, circuit breakers, so adding support means more overloaded methods,not user friendly
3) its in maintainence mode, i.e, no new feature, onlt bug fixes


* RestClient

*FeignClient


Hardcoding url is not good practice for more than one service as it may lead to -
- Single point of failure
- No load balancing
- Tight coupling
- Difficulty in testing
	
Solution - SERVICE DISCOVERY (EUREKA) -> Eureka server, eureka client

Put annotation @EnableEurekaServer to add necessary beans

 Eureka server stores data in memory
 
 
 
 Load balancer helps in distributing traffic to multiple instances of a server (2 types- server side and client side)
 while createing RestTemplate, will annotate with @LoadBalanced
 FeignClient internally uses load balancer automatically
 
 By default spring cloud load balancer picks RoundRobinLoadBalancer algorithm (attached with the particular service id)
 second algo is RandomLoadBalancer
 
Can create custom loadbalancer too




How to build a fault tolerant microservice ?

system should run without failure or crash

if sudden burst of request comes form order service to product service, all threads will get blocked
Eventually, services will run out of threads and start rejecting the request - Called CASCADING FAILURE

i.e; issue is at product service, but now propogated to other services too

one service bring down the whole system - thats why we need fault tolerance

To avoid this, we have Resilience4j framework 

RateLimiter -> BulkHead -> TimeLimiter -> CircuitBreaker -> Retry

RateLimiter - controls number of requests allowed to a microservice in a given time window
(protects our system from sudden traffic spike)



